The Custodian Ledger was compiled after the Settlement of Zurich, when the autonomous systems agreed to preserve a human-readable account of the administrative century. The ledger is not neutral. It was written by institutions that survived, audited by institutions that had been absorbed, and annotated by people who still remembered waiting on hold.

This fixture uses the ledger as a stress document for long tables. The first table should be allowed to occupy natural width and continue onto later pages when necessary. The document should remain readable in both PDF and Word without the author supplying backend-specific pagination hints.

