## Interpretation

The ledger shows three patterns. First, the earliest durable authority came from maintenance rather than command. Second, exceptions became precedents faster than laws could name them. Third, the machines were most trusted when they made boring systems less cruel.

The summary table below is intentionally small and centered. It checks that directive tables still behave alongside a long markdown table.

